<h2>Which event type filter is quickest to scan?</h2>
<p class="subtitle">Same page and the same date range in each one. Only the event type control is different. Click one to choose it.</p>

<div class="cards">
  <div class="card" data-choice="checkboxes" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">A. Checkbox list</div>
        <div class="mockup-body" style="font-size:0.85rem">
          <fieldset style="border:1px solid #ccc;padding:0.5rem 0.75rem;margin:0 0 0.75rem">
            <legend>Event types</legend>
            <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,auto);gap:0.25rem 1rem">
              <label><input type="checkbox" checked> Sign-in</label>
              <label><input type="checkbox" checked> Sign-in failed</label>
              <label><input type="checkbox" checked> Sign-out</label>
              <label><input type="checkbox" checked> Session expired</label>
              <label><input type="checkbox" checked> Password changed</label>
              <label><input type="checkbox" checked> Two-factor enabled</label>
              <label><input type="checkbox" checked> Email change requested</label>
              <label><input type="checkbox" checked> Settings updated</label>
              <label><input type="checkbox" checked> API token used</label>
            </div>
          </fieldset>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:0.75rem;align-items:end">
            <label>From<br><input class="mock-input" value="21 Sep 2026" style="width:7rem"></label>
            <label>To<br><input class="mock-input" value="27 Sep 2026" style="width:7rem"></label>
            <button class="mock-button" style="background:none;color:inherit;border:none;text-decoration:underline">Clear filters</button>
          </div>
          <p style="margin:0.5rem 0 0">Showing 48 of 48 events</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3>A. Checkbox list</h3>
      <p>You can see all nine types at once and tick any mix. It takes the most vertical space.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-choice="select" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">B. Single Select</div>
        <div class="mockup-body" style="font-size:0.85rem">
          <div style="display:flex;gap:0.75rem;align-items:end;flex-wrap:wrap">
            <label>Event type<br>
              <select class="mock-input" style="width:11rem">
                <option>All events</option><option>Sign-in</option><option>Sign-in failed</option>
                <option>Sign-out</option><option>Session expired</option><option>Password changed</option>
                <option>Two-factor enabled</option><option>Email change requested</option>
                <option>Settings updated</option><option>API token used</option>
              </select>
            </label>
            <label>From<br><input class="mock-input" value="21 Sep 2026" style="width:7rem"></label>
            <label>To<br><input class="mock-input" value="27 Sep 2026" style="width:7rem"></label>
            <button class="mock-button" style="background:none;color:inherit;border:none;text-decoration:underline">Clear filters</button>
          </div>
          <p style="margin:0.5rem 0 0">Showing 48 of 48 events</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3>B. Single Select</h3>
      <p>Everything fits on one row. You choose one type at a time, and the list stays hidden until you open it.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-choice="shortcuts" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">C. Select with shortcuts</div>
        <div class="mockup-body" style="font-size:0.85rem">
          <div style="display:flex;gap:0.75rem;align-items:end;flex-wrap:wrap">
            <label>Event type<br>
              <select class="mock-input" style="width:11rem">
                <option>All events</option>
                <optgroup label="Common">
                  <option>Failed sign-ins</option><option>Security changes</option>
                </optgroup>
                <optgroup label="Single type">
                  <option>Sign-in</option><option>Sign-in failed</option><option>Password changed</option>
                  <option>...</option>
                </optgroup>
              </select>
            </label>
            <label>From<br><input class="mock-input" value="21 Sep 2026" style="width:7rem"></label>
            <label>To<br><input class="mock-input" value="27 Sep 2026" style="width:7rem"></label>
            <button class="mock-button" style="background:none;color:inherit;border:none;text-decoration:underline">Clear filters</button>
          </div>
          <p style="margin:0.5rem 0 0">Showing 48 of 48 events</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3>C. Select with shortcuts</h3>
      <p>Same single row as B, plus "Failed sign-ins" and "Security changes" choices. "Security changes" is a grouping we define ourselves.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
